  "paper_id": "osdi-2026-continuation-centric-computing-with-arca-0b6a98ab",
  "title": "Continuation-Centric Computing with Arca",
  "abstract": "This paper presents continuation-centric computing, an operating system design paradigm for “serverless”-style workloads: short-lived tasks that spend a substantial fraction of time waiting on dependencies and other services. Under this paradigm, a running function can capture its current continuation—a lightweight snapshot of its state—as a distinct function that can be paused, migrated, or copied as needed.\n\nThis paper evaluates the continuation-centric computing model using Arca, an operating system providing continuation capture as a core service. Arca supports a process abstraction that is broadly similar to Unix processes in guarantees and isolation, but additionally provides efficient capture and resumption of serializable, portable continuations.",
